Z||000000||John E. Rowlett||07-05-2001||05:36 PM||||I saw a post recently about location of oil pressure switch on engine. Thsi weekend I put my gt up on my floor jack and crawled around, under, and trough and cannot find it. Help! <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||07-05-2001||05:40 PM||||Look from the top. It's mounted on a tube on the front of the engine in the general area of the water pump.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000002||John E. Rowlett||07-05-2001||05:55 PM||||thanks for your response, I will look tonight.||||reg||10
Z||000003||LarryB||07-06-2001||12:45 AM||||Here are a couple of pictures, <BR>you can see the silver fitting just above the "B" in the first picture below. The 2nd pic shows a new sensor before the wiring harness is reinstalled.<BR> <A HREF="http://fiero.xcom.net/fiero1a.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero.xcom.net/fiero1a.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://fiero.xcom.net/fiero2a.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero.xcom.net/fiero2a.jpg</A> <P>This is on a V6 with factory A/C. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||07-06-2001||02:18 AM||||in this picture you can see the oil pressure sending unit on the long tube running from the side of the block. This is the '88 style sending unit, the one for the '86 will be larger but it mounts in the same location.....in this picture it is the silver tubular object in the top left of the photo.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-399f.jpg"> ||||reg||1
